### Claims platform — full happy path through the gateway (docker compose -f deployment/docker-compose.yml up -d --build)
### Run top to bottom in IntelliJ HTTP Client or VS Code REST Client (response handlers use the IntelliJ syntax).
### Stage numbers follow the business flow: report -> pick up -> info request -> assess & decide -> approve -> settle.

@gw = http://localhost:8000
@claims = http://localhost:8080

### 0a. Customer logs in
POST {{claims}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "priya", "password": "ChangeMe123!"}

> {% client.global.set("priya", response.body.access_token); %}

### 0b. Handler, team lead, manager log in
POST {{claims}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "arun", "password": "ChangeMe123!"}

> {% client.global.set("arun", response.body.access_token); %}

###
POST {{claims}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "meera", "password": "ChangeMe123!"}

> {% client.global.set("meera", response.body.access_token); %}

###
POST {{claims}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "lee", "password": "ChangeMe123!"}

> {% client.global.set("lee", response.body.access_token); %}

### Stage 1.2 — C1: my policies for the "Report an incident" form (Policy system, cached 5 min)
GET {{gw}}/claimant/v1/policies
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}

### Stage 1.4 — C2: ask for a secure upload link
POST {{gw}}/claimant/v1/uploads
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"fileName": "dashcam.jpg", "contentType": "image/jpeg", "sizeBytes": 11}

> {%
    client.global.set("uploadId", response.body.uploadId);
    client.global.set("uploadUrl", response.body.uploadUrl);
%}

### ... the app PUTs the file straight to storage
PUT {{uploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

hello photo

### Stage 1.5 — C3: submit the claim (cover check inline; returns the claim number)
POST {{gw}}/claimant/v1/claims
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{$uuid}}
X-Correlation-Id: demo-happy-path

{
  "policyNumber": "SG-MTR-POL-1001",
  "lineOfBusiness": "MOTOR",
  "incidentAt": "2026-11-10T09:00:00Z",
  "incident": {
    "peril": "COLLISION",
    "description": "Rear-ended at the traffic lights",
    "location": "Orchard Road",
    "vehicleRegistration": "SBA1234X",
    "driverName": "Priya Nair",
    "damageDescription": "Rear bumper and boot",
    "thirdParties": [{"name": "John Lim", "vehicleRegistration": "SGX9876Z", "insurer": "NTUC Income"}]
  },
  "claimedAmount": {"amount": "6000.00", "currency": "SGD"},
  "uploadIds": ["{{uploadId}}"],
  "contact": {"phone": "+6591234567"}
}

> {%
    client.global.set("claimId", response.body.claimId);
    client.global.set("claimNumber", response.body.claimNumber);
%}

### Stage 1.7 — Notifications: "We have received your claim ..." (a second or two later)
GET {{gw}}/claimant/v1/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}

### Stage 2.8 — I1: the handler's work queue (Insights), oldest SLA first
GET {{gw}}/staff/v1/work-queue?view=unassigned&market=SG
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}

### S2: claim workspace; ETag = version for the next If-Match
GET {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}

> {% client.global.set("etag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag")); %}

### Stage 2.9 — S4: pick up (a second handler doing this now gets 409 CLAIM_ALREADY_ASSIGNED)
POST {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/assignment
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}
If-Match: {{etag}}

> {% client.global.set("etag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag")); %}

### Stage 2.10 — S5: start the review
POST {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/start-assessment
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}
If-Match: {{etag}}

> {% client.global.set("etag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag")); %}

### Stage 2.11 — S6: initial reserve SGD 5,000 (manager's "money at risk" updates)
POST {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/reserves
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}
If-Match: {{etag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": {"amount": "5000.00", "currency": "SGD"}, "reason": "Initial estimate"}

> {% client.global.set("etag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag")); %}

### Stage 3.12 — S7: request information (claim AWAITING_INFO, SLA paused)
POST {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/info-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}
If-Match: {{etag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"items": ["Police report", "Repair quote"]}

> {% client.global.set("requestId", response.body.result); %}

### Stage 3.13 — C7: the customer sees what is needed
GET {{gw}}/claimant/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/info-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}

### Stage 3.14 — C8: the customer answers (back to UNDER_ASSESSMENT, SLA resumes)
POST {{gw}}/claimant/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/info-requests/{{requestId}}/responses
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"answer": "Police report PR-2026-1182 and the workshop quote are attached", "uploadIds": []}

### refresh the ETag after the customer's change
GET {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}

> {% client.global.set("etag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag")); %}

### Stage 4.15 — S8: assessment, and the reserve follows the repair quote
POST {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}
If-Match: {{etag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"liability": "FULL", "assessedAmount": {"amount": "12000.00", "currency": "SGD"}, "notes": "Third party at fault, CCTV confirms"}

> {% client.global.set("etag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag")); %}

###
POST {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/reserves
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}
If-Match: {{etag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": {"amount": "12000.00", "currency": "SGD"}, "reason": "Repair quote received"}

> {% client.global.set("etag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag")); %}

### Stage 4.16-17 — S9: propose approval of SGD 12,000 (above Arun's SGD 10,000 limit -> 202, DECISION_PENDING)
POST {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/decisions
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}
If-Match: {{etag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"outcome": "APPROVE", "amount": {"amount": "12000.00", "currency": "SGD"}}

> {%
    client.global.set("decisionId", response.body.result.decisionId);
    client.global.set("etag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag"));
%}

### I3: the team lead's approvals inbox (Insights)
GET {{gw}}/staff/v1/approvals
Authorization: Bearer {{meera}}

### S10: the team lead approves (Arun approving his own proposal would get 403 SELF_APPROVAL_NOT_ALLOWED)
POST {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/decisions/{{decisionId}}/approval
Authorization: Bearer {{meera}}
If-Match: {{etag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"action": "APPROVE"}

> {% client.global.set("etag", response.headers.valueOf("ETag")); %}

### Stage 5.19 — S11: instruct payment (Payments simulator answers on Kafka; account ending 0000 would fail)
POST {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/settlements
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}
If-Match: {{etag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"payee": {"name": "Priya Nair", "bankCode": "DBSSSGSG", "accountNumber": "123456789"}, "amount": {"amount": "12000.00", "currency": "SGD"}}

### Stage 5.20 — a few seconds later: SETTLED, reserve released
GET {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}

### Stage 5.21 — the customer is told: "SGD 12000.00 has been paid to your account"
GET {{gw}}/claimant/v1/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}

### C5 / C6: what the customer sees (no reserves, no internal steps)
GET {{gw}}/claimant/v1/claims/{{claimId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}

###
GET {{gw}}/claimant/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/timeline
Authorization: Bearer {{priya}}

### S3: the full internal audit trail
GET {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}

### N5: what was sent to the customer and whether it was delivered
GET {{gw}}/staff/v1/claims/{{claimId}}/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{arun}}

### Dashboards (Insights): exposure, workload, performance, SLA
GET {{gw}}/staff/v1/insights/exposure?market=SG
Authorization: Bearer {{lee}}

###
GET {{gw}}/staff/v1/insights/workload
Authorization: Bearer {{meera}}

###
GET {{gw}}/staff/v1/insights/sla?market=SG
Authorization: Bearer {{meera}}

### Stage 6.22 — closure happens automatically after the 14-day cooling-off (daily auto-close job)
